---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import ImageToolPageFrame from '../components/ImageToolPageFrame.astro';
import ImageToolGrid from '../components/ImageToolGrid.astro';
import FaqList from '../components/FaqList.astro';
import { REMOVE_WATERMARK_TOOL } from '../config/image-tools';
import { REMOVE_WATERMARK_FAQ } from '../content/remove-watermark-faq';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
const tool = REMOVE_WATERMARK_TOOL;
const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'WebApplication', name: 'ConvertAnyFile Remove Watermark', url: `${SITE.origin}/remove-watermark/`, applicationCategory: 'MultimediaApplication', operatingSystem: 'Any', offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
  featureList: ['Local browser processing','Up to 50 images per batch','Automatic shared or individual editing recommendation','Rectangle mask','Circle mask','Square mask','Diamond mask','4-Point Star mask','Solid manual text-shaped mask','Move, resize and rotate masks','Per-image mask overrides','Cancelable sequential processing','ZIP download','JPG, PNG and WebP input','No image upload'],
};
---
<SiteLayout title={tool.title} description={tool.description} schema={schema}>
  <ImageToolPageFrame tool={tool} />
  <section class="content-wide-section white gemini-content-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="content-intro-grid"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">One editor, one image or a batch</span><h2>Start with one shared mask, or give every image its own.</h2><p>Add one image or up to 50. If the current batch shares an aspect ratio, the editor starts with One mask for all. Mixed layouts start with Edit individually. The toggle remains available, so the automatic choice never locks you into a workflow.</p></div><div class="content-summary-card"><strong>Browser-only processing</strong><p>Decoding, mask interaction, visible-pixel repair, output encoding, and ZIP creation happen locally. Images are not uploaded to a watermark-removal API.</p></div></div><ul class="content-checklist"><li>Up to 50 JPG, PNG, or WebP images; 10 MB per source image and 200 MB total source input.</li><li>Same-ratio batches default to one normalized shared mask for repeated placement.</li><li>Mixed ratios stay in the batch and default to individual masks instead of being rejected.</li><li>Move, resize, and rotate masks after drawing; switch to individual mode to customize only exceptions.</li><li>Cancel a long run without discarding successful results that already finished.</li></ul></div></section>
  <section class="content-wide-section gemini-content-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">Six manual masks</span><h2>Match the mask to the visible watermark instead of painting a giant box.</h2><p>The repair engine only changes pixels covered by masks you create. Tighter selection usually gives nearby pixels more useful context for repair. Every mask can be moved, resized, and rotated after creation.</p></div><div class="comparison-table-wrap"><table class="comparison-table"><thead><tr><th>Mask</th><th>Best starting point</th><th>Behavior</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Rectangle</strong></td><td>Wide labels, corner badges, horizontal marks</td><td>Free width and height · rotatable</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Circle</strong></td><td>Round logos or compact glow</td><td>Locked circular footprint · rotatable</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Square</strong></td><td>Square icons and compact app-style marks</td><td>Locked 1:1 footprint · rotatable</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Diamond</strong></td><td>Rotated-square badges and diagonal marks</td><td>Locked diamond footprint · rotatable</td></tr><tr><td><strong>4-Point Star</strong></td><td>Sparkle-style marks</td><td>Locked four-point footprint · rotatable</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Text</strong></td><td>Visible word, number, or phrase watermarks</td><td>Solid bold glyph mask · auto-sized · rotatable</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></section>
  <section class="content-wide-section white gemini-content-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="content-intro-grid"><div><span class="section-kicker">Text mask</span><h2>Type the visible watermark, then position the solid mask over the characters.</h2><p>Choose Text and enter a visible word, number, or phrase. The editor creates a solid bold text-shaped mask and automatically sizes its bounding box to the content, so a short value such as a single digit can still be dragged close to an image edge.</p><p>Drag the mask to move it, use the square corner handles to resize it, and drag the round handle to rotate it over diagonal text. This is intentionally manual: it does not run OCR, guess which text should disappear, or scan the image for words.</p></div><div class="content-summary-card"><strong>When Text works best</strong><p>Use Text when the visible mark follows recognizable characters. For heavily stylized lettering, large glow, thick shadows, or artwork around the text, add a shape mask that covers the remaining visible pixels.</p></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="content-wide-section gemini-content-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">Move, resize, rotate</span><h2>Use the mask handles instead of redrawing every adjustment.</h2><p>Click or tap an existing mask to select it. Drag inside the mask to move it, drag a square corner handle to resize it, or drag the round handle above the selection to rotate it. Rotation is preserved in shared copies and per-image custom masks.</p></div><div class="callout"><strong>Edge placement stays practical</strong><p>Short Text masks are sized from their actual content instead of a fixed wide box. That leaves enough room to drag a digit or short word toward a corner without the invisible selection bounds stopping early.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="content-wide-section white gemini-content-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">Shared or individual</span><h2>Batch fast when placement repeats. Customize when it does not.</h2><p>A shared mask is stored as normalized coordinates plus its rotation, so it scales with different pixel dimensions that use the same layout. If a few images differ, switch to Edit individually and adjust only those images. The queue marks shared copies, custom masks, and images that still need a mask.</p></div><div class="callout"><strong>Same ratio is helpful, but position still matters</strong><p>One mask for all is most reliable when the watermark appears at the same relative position, angle, and approximate size. A matching aspect ratio does not guarantee identical placement.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="content-wide-section gemini-content-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">Visible-pixel repair</span><h2>Know what the browser can and cannot reconstruct.</h2><p>The current non-AI repair estimates selected pixels from nearby unmasked pixels. Small marks over smooth or repeated backgrounds are usually easier than large marks crossing faces, hair, text, architecture edges, or unique objects. Keep the original and inspect the After preview before reuse.</p></div><div class="callout"><strong>Use only on images you have the right to edit</strong><p>The tool changes visible pixels. It does not claim to remove invisible provenance, Content Credentials, metadata-based authenticity information, or SynthID-style signals.</p></div></div></section>
  <section class="content-wide-section white gemini-content-section"><div class="site-container"><FaqList items={REMOVE_WATERMARK_FAQ} title="Remove Watermark FAQ" intro="Batch behavior, six mask types, solid text masks, move/resize/rotate interaction, local processing, output quality, ZIP download, and visible-pixel limitations." /></div></section>
  <section class="content-wide-section gemini-content-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">Learn more</span><h2>Guides for shape selection, text watermarks, and focused AI-logo editing.</h2><p>Use the guides when you need a workflow explanation before editing a larger batch.</p></div><div class="category-grid"><a class="category-card category-card--live" href="/guides/how-to-remove-watermark-from-image/"><div class="category-icon">G</div><div><span class="live-badge">Guide</span><h3>How to remove a visible watermark</h3><p>Choose a mask, position and rotate it, decide shared vs individual editing, and review quality.</p></div><span class="category-arrow">→</span></a><a class="category-card category-card--live" href="/guides/how-to-remove-text-watermark-from-image/"><div class="category-icon">T</div><div><span class="live-badge">Guide</span><h3>How to use a text-shaped mask</h3><p>Type visible text, move/resize/rotate the solid mask, and understand where manual text masking works best.</p></div><span class="category-arrow">→</span></a></div><div class="section-heading wide" style="margin-top:36px"><span class="section-kicker">Related Image Tools</span><h2>Use the focused Gemini tool when two simple shapes are enough.</h2></div><ImageToolGrid compact /></div></section>
</SiteLayout>
